<title>USA: Weekend box office chart -- Dec 13-15.</title>
<headline>Weekend box office chart -- Dec 13-15.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the December 13-15 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Jerry Maguire	    $17,084,296	 $  ----</p>
<p>2. Mars Attacks!	     $9,384,272	 $  ----</p>
<p>3. 101 Dalmatians	    $8,932,970	 $ 75,575,864</p>
<p>4. The Preacher's Wife     $7,649,752	 $  ----</p>
<p>5. Daylight		    $4,137,210	 $ 16,653,910</p>
<p>6. Jingle All the Way	$4,052,053	 $ 43,324,886</p>
<p>7. Star Trek:</p>
<p>   First Contact	     $3,432,345	 $ 76,721,064</p>
<p>8. Ransom			$2,979,816	 $117,504,943</p>
<p>9. Space Jam		   $2,347,556	 $ 76,536,367</p>
<p>10 The English Patient     $1,779,831	 $ 16,015,227</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. &quot;Mars Attacks!&quot; and &quot;Space Jam&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc. . &quot;101 Dalmatians,&quot; The Preacher's Wife&quot; and &quot;Ransom&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Daylight&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd. . &quot;Jingle All the Way&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp.. &quot;Star Trek: First Contact&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;The English Patient&quot; is released by Disney-owned Miramax Films.</p>
